%% Phase 4 (password change) and Phase 5 (revocation / re-issue)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SD as Smart Device
    participant AS as Authentication Server
    actor ADM as Admin (office)

    Note over U,SD: Phase 4 — only after a successful online login in the same session<br/>(the AS has proven A is correct, so a fuzzy-verifier false accept cannot corrupt the card)
    U->>SD: PW_U' (new password)
    SD->>SD: r' ← random, RPW' = h(PW_U' ‖ r')
    SD->>SD: B' = A ⊕ h(ID_U ‖ RPW')<br/>V' = int(h(h(ID_U ‖ RPW'))) mod n0
    SD->>SD: card ← {B', V', r'} (TID, n0, pk_AS, Q_AS kept)
    Note over SD,AS: AS not involved, A unchanged

    Note over ADM,AS: Phase 5 — revocation (lost card, student left the course)
    ADM->>AS: revoke ID_U → revoked = 1
    Note over AS: later logins with that card fail at Step 4.4

    Note over ADM,AS: Phase 5 — re-issue a card (D2)
    U->>SD: new device: r'' ← random, RPW'' = h(PW_U ‖ r'')
    SD->>AS: {ID_U, RPW''} (secure channel)
    AS->>AS: v ← v + 1, A' = h(ID_U ‖ x ‖ v)<br/>TID_cur ← new TID, TID_old ← ⊥<br/>revoked = 0, failed_attempts = 0
    AS->>SD: {B'', V'', TID, n0, pk_AS, Q_AS}
    Note over AS: old card: its TID is unknown and its A is stale<br/>→ useless even if the password is known
